Subject: module-allow-symbol-crc-mismatch

Let a module load when a symbol CRC disagrees with the kernel, and say
'(allowed)' in the warning so the bypass is visible in dmesg. The vendor
modules are built against the stock kernel; which of their symbol CRCs
differ from this build's has not been inventoried, so the check is
relaxed rather than shown unnecessary. This is an accepted risk.

Upstream: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common commit 5c5f2fea42dd4cc5ae1002945d86e305c09d3262
License: GPL-2.0-or-later, matching kernel/module/version.c

--- a/kernel/module/version.c
+++ b/kernel/module/version.c
@@ -68,8 +68,8 @@
 	return 1;
 
 bad_version:
-	pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s\n", info->name, symname);
-	return 0;
+	pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s (allowed)\n", info->name, symname);
+	return 1;
 }
 
 int check_modstruct_version(const struct load_info *info,
